  "plan": {
    "goal": "Perfuse a liver-on-chip so hepatocytes experience the in vivo hepatic sinusoidal wall shear stress (~0.1 Pa, mid-range of 0.05-0.15 Pa).",
    "rationale": "Hepatic sinusoidal wall shear stress is very low, 0.05-0.15 Pa (cell_physiology registry for HepG2, liver). I target the mid-range 0.1 Pa. A wide, shallow channel (1000 um wide x 100 um high x 20 mm long) is a standard liver-OOC geometry. flow_rate_for_shear_stress gives 10 uL/min for 0.1 Pa at water-like medium viscosity (1e-3 Pa.s). Verified: wall_shear_stress(10 uL/min) = 0.100 Pa; Reynolds ~0.30 (deeply laminar, <<2300); residence time ~12 s per pass; pressure drop ~40 Pa (trivially supplied by a syringe pump); O2 supply/demand ratio ~56 (no hypoxia for 20,000 cells at ~0.03 fmol/s/cell). Cells: HepG2 (BSL-1, liver) seeded at 1e5 cells/cm2 on 0.2 cm2 = 20,000 cells, cultured 72 h (within the 48-60 h doubling window to reach a confluent monolayer). Medium viscosity assumed water-like (1e-3 Pa.s).",
